users/b4snet/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/b4snet/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/b4snet/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/b4snet/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/b4snet","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/b4snet/swasthya-nepal/commits/48913ae83e0b25d62464199903a721638fe89d45/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T04:18:29Z","email":"dipsonbasnet95@gmail.com","name":"Dipson Basnet"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T04:18:29Z","email":"dipsonbasnet95@gmail.com","name":"Dipson Basnet"},"message":"feat(auth): token refresh via httpOnly cookie; forgot/reset password pages\n\nMove the access token strictly to memory and deliver the refresh token ONLY via\nthe httpOnly swasthya_refresh cookie (SECURITY.md 4/23), removing the previous\nlocalStorage/sessionStorage persistence and the JS-exposed refresh token. On\npage reload the SPA calls POST /auth/refresh with no body and the browser sends\nthe cookie. Proactive refresh uses the absolute expiry recorded at issuance.\nnoRefresh marks the refresh path so a 401 there cannot loop.\n\nAdd staff forgot-password and reset-password pages wired to the generic\ndescription endpoints. Update the affected test suites (LoginPage, session\nexpiry, auth-session, api-client-auth, TenantContext, Audit, e2e dashboard) for\nthe mount cookie-refresh, and reset the in-memory token store between test files\nto fix single-thread cross-file leakage.","tree":{"sha":"fac6d656df17c6a5bc782e4a3c3ca39c2080aed2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/b4snet/swasthya-nepal/git/trees/fac6d656df17c6a5bc782e4a3c3ca39c2080aed2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/b4snet/swasthya-nepal/git/commits/48913ae83e0b25d62464199903a721638fe89d45","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"ava