{"author":{"date":"2026-08-27T12:03:27Z","email":"dipsonbasnet95@gmail.com","name":"Dipson Basnet"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-27T12:03:27Z","email":"dipsonbasnet95@gmail.com","name":"Dipson Basnet"},"message":"feat(ux): introduce contextual domain command navigation\n\nReplace legacy module navigation with context-aware domain launchers.\nWhen a user clicks a domain in the sidebar, a contextual command surface\nreveals real operational entry points instead of navigating to a generic page.\n\nArchitecture: DOMAIN → CONTEXT → AVAILABLE WORK → ACTION → RESULT\n\nNew components:\n- DomainCommandSurface: contextual command tile grid that appears when\n  a domain is clicked, showing role-aware operational entry points\n- Each tile shows: icon, label, purpose, optional count/status\n- Tiles are keyboard-navigable with arrow keys and Escape to close\n- Click-outside closes the surface\n- Focus returns properly on close\n\nIntegration:\n- Sidebar click now opens DomainCommandSurface for domains with children\n- Dashboard (no children) still navigates directly\n- Surface closes on route change\n- Surface appears above page content in the main content area\n\nDesign decisions:\n- Light-only (no dark mode)\n- Grid layout: auto-fill tiles at 200px min-width\n- Semantic tones: normal, warning, critical, info\n- Priority levels: primary (teal), secondary (neutral), exception (red)\n- Respects prefers-reduced-motion\n- Accessible: role=navigation, aria-label, keyboard arrow navigation\n- Responsive: stacked on mobile, 2-col on tablet, grid on desktop\n- Touch targets ≥ 44px\n\nTypeScript: 0 errors\nFrontend tests: 188/188 pass\nBuild: passes\n\n🤖 Generated with Codebuff\nCo-Authored-By: Codebuff <noreply@codebuff.com>","tree":{"sha":"293e3a23607138875b375f71e6562e0af9d15888","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/b4snet/swasthya-nepal/git/trees/293e3a23607138875b375f71e6562e0af9d15888"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/b4snet/swasthya-nepal/git/commits/88a8cefe