ring framework, hospital capacity model, and capacity tests\n\nPhase 93 — Scale and Capacity Engineering.\n\nAdd comprehensive scale and capacity engineering framework:\n\nScaleEngineeringService:\n- Database capacity analysis (tables, indexes, RLS, connections)\n- RLS policy inventory by table with command breakdown\n- Index audit for major tables (patient, encounter, order, etc.)\n- Connection capacity analysis with utilization monitoring\n- Hospital capacity model (small/medium/large/multi-facility)\n- Patient search performance baseline\n- RLS overhead estimation (794 policies ≈ 10% overhead)\n- Tenant skew analysis for noisy-neighbor detection\n- Full scale summary for current database\n\nHospital Capacity Model:\n- Small Hospital (50-100 beds): 80 registrations/day\n- Medium Hospital (200-400 beds): 300 registrations/day\n- Large Hospital (500+ beds): 600 registrations/day\n- Multi-Facility (1000+ beds): 1000+ registrations/day\n\nSCALE_ENGINEERING.md:\n- Scale targets and workload profiles\n- Database baseline (236 tables, 794 policies, 875 indexes)\n- PostgreSQL configuration (dev/staging/production)\n- RLS performance analysis (GUC-based, ~10% overhead)\n- Patient search scale (pg_trgm for 10K+ patients)\n- Connection capacity and pooling recommendations\n- Data growth model (monthly/yearly projections)\n- API throughput estimates by endpoint\n- Noisy-neighbor analysis and mitigation\n- Scale classification: small/medium ready, large/multi with conditions\n- Bottleneck analysis with mitigations\n- Scaling decisions with evidence\n\nScale Tests:\n- 9 tests (674 assertions)\n- Database capacity measurement\n- RLS policy inventory\n- Index audit\n- Connection capacity analysis\n- Hospital capacity model\n- RLS overhead estimation\n- Tenant skew analysis\n- Patient search performance\n- Full scale summary\n\nVerified current state:\n- PostgreSQL 17.6, 236 tables, 794 RLS policies\n- 875 indexes, 6 helper functions\n- 100 max connections, ~5% utilization\n- All health checks pass\n- All backend tests pass\n\n🤖 Generated with Codebuff\nCo-Authored-By: Codebuff <noreply@codebuff.com>","tree":{"sha":"0356d907e4afd0ecb59611926584dbf53645e950","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/b4snet/swasthya-nepal/git/trees/0356d907e4afd0ecb59611926584dbf53645e950"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/b4snet/swasthya-nepal/git/commits/0e205c36a72b112a743c214c6af9015b3ccb5569","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/260671858?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/b4snet/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/b4snet/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/b4snet/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/b4snet/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/b4snet","id":260671858,"login":"b4snet","node_id":"U_kgDOD4mJcg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/b4snet/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/b4snet/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/b4snet/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/b4snet/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/b4snet/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/b4snet","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/b4snet/swasthya-nepal/commit/0e205c36a72b112a743c214c6af9015b3ccb5569","node_id":"C_kwDOT01FpdoAKDBlMjA1YzM2YTcyYjExMmE3NDNjMjE0YzZhZjkwMTViM2NjYjU1Njk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/b4snet/swasthya-nepal/commit/f62ff206b9805dd890d8ea460e45550cddf56acb","sha":"f62ff206b9805dd890d8ea460e45550cddf56acb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/b4snet/swasthya-nepal/commits/f62ff206b9805dd890d8ea460e45550cddf56acb"}],"sha":"0e205c36a72b112a743c214c6af9015b3ccb5569","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/b4snet/swasthya-nepal/commits/0e205c36a72b112a743c214c6af9015b3ccb5569"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/260671858?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/b4snet/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/b4snet/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/b4snet/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/b4snet/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/b4snet","id":260671858,"login":"b4snet","node_id":"U_kgDOD4mJcg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/b4snet/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/b4snet/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/b4snet/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/b4snet/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/b4snet/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/b4snet","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/b4snet/swasthya-nepal/commits/f62ff206b9805dd890d8ea460e45550cddf56acb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T16:59:24Z","email":"dipsonbasnet95@gmail.com","name":"Dipson Basnet"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T16:59:24Z","email":"dipsonbasnet95@gmail.com","name":"Dipson Basnet"},"message":"docs: add resilience framework, recovery runbooks, and chaos matrix\n\nPhase 92 — Disaster Recovery and Business Continuity.\n\nAdd comprehensive disaster recovery and business continuity framework:\n\nResilienceService:\n- Health check: database, RLS, Redis, queue dependency verification\n- Data integrity: verify critical tables accessible\n- Post-restore RLS verification: MANDATORY after any restore\n- Recovery verification recording in audit trail\n- Graceful handling when Redis not configured\n\nDISASTER_RECOVERY.md:\n- Resilience model: failure → detect → protect → contain → recover\n- RTO/RPO targets: database 30min/0, app 5min/0, Redis 5min/0\n- Criticality matrix: clinical CRITICAL, billing MEDIUM, AI LOW\n- Dependency map with single points of failure identified\n- 8 failure scenarios with detection, recovery, and RTO\n- Database recovery: PITR restore → roles.sql → migrate → grants.sql\n- Downtime procedures: paper forms, reconciliation workflow\n- Business continuity runbook: recovery sequence\n- Chaos matrix: all scenarios with measured RTO/RPO\n- Recovery priority order: database → auth → clinical → billing\n- Security during recovery: RLS never disabled\n- AI degradation: core HMS continues when AI fails\n- Backup strategy: Supabase PITR + daily, source in Git\n- Tenant isolation under failure: blast radius analysis\n\nResilience Tests:\n- 7 tests (32 assertions)\n- Comprehensive health check (DB, RLS, Redis, queue)\n- RLS integrity with 700+ policies\n- swasthya_app NOBYPASSRLS verification\n- Data integrity across critical tables\n- Post-restore RLS verification\n- Audit events table accessibility\n- RLS function presence check\n\nVerified existing resilience capabilities:\n- Health endpoints: /health/live, /health/ready\n- Database: Supabase PITR 7-day (paid)\n- Docker: restart unless-stopped\n- Queue: database-backed (persistent)\n- Security: RLS, NOBYPASSRLS, least-privilege role\n\nVerification results:\n- Backend unit tests: 28/28 (149 assertions)\n- Backend resilience tests: 7/7 (32 assertions)\n- Backend Pint: 1063 files clean\n- Frontend tests: 188/188\n- Frontend TypeScript: 0 errors\n\n🤖 Generated with Codebuff\nCo-Authored-By: Codebuff <noreply@codebuff.com>","tree":{"sha":"be6e37ac9f0c5d4a77a0a67993aeaf607ec9ea27","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/b4snet/swasthya-nepal/git/trees/be6e37ac9f0c5d4a77a0a67993aeaf607ec9ea27"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/b4snet/swasthya-nepal/git/commits/f62ff206b9805dd890d8ea460e45550cddf56acb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2