bkincz/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkincz/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkincz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkincz/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkincz","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bkincz/conduit/commits/0c2a0d05682f57f8ca633b4f245c619329795082/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T09:49:41Z","email":"beni.kinczel@gmail.com","name":"Beni K"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T09:49:41Z","email":"beni.kinczel@gmail.com","name":"Beni K"},"message":"feat: set up comprehensive CI and automated release pipeline\n\nThis commit introduces a robust CI/CD system to improve code quality, ensure package integrity, and automate the release process.\n\nKey changes include:\n- **Comprehensive CI:** The previous `verify` job is split into `test`, `build`, and `smoke`. The `test` job now runs across multiple operating systems (Ubuntu, Windows) and Node.js versions (22, 24).\n- **Package Smoke Test:** A new `smoke` job verifies that the built and packaged artifact can be installed, its exports resolved (ESM and CJS), and its type definitions correctly interpreted by a consumer project. This prevents publishing broken packages.\n- **Automated Release Workflow:** A new `release` workflow triggers on version tag pushes, automatically validating the tag against the package version, publishing to npm, and creating a GitHub release.\n- Updated all GitHub Actions to their latest major versions for improved stability and features.","tree":{"sha":"2b032fb5eb2ee3745f1e6896bebfa8108aec43c6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bkincz/conduit/git/trees/2b032fb5eb2ee3745f1e6896bebfa8108aec43c6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bkincz/conduit/git/commits/0c2a0d05682f57f8ca633b4f245c619329795082","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":fal