,"node_id":"C_kwDOT1kFAdoAKGNjMTNiYjVmOGI2NmY0OTYzMjM0NDQ3ZjA2NzE2OTFjMTgxOTJjY2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NEARBuilders/nostr.nearbuilders.org/commit/4e03935799fb0c09b126b422aca986cb0d5a8765","sha":"4e03935799fb0c09b126b422aca986cb0d5a8765","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/nostr.nearbuilders.org/commits/4e03935799fb0c09b126b422aca986cb0d5a8765"}],"sha":"cc13bb5f8b66f4963234447f0671691c18192cca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/nostr.nearbuilders.org/commits/cc13bb5f8b66f4963234447f0671691c18192cca"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41765025?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kampouse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kampouse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kampouse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kampouse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Kampouse","id":41765025,"login":"Kampouse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxNzY1MDI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kampouse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kampouse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kampouse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kampouse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kampouse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kampouse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/nostr.nearbuilders.org/commits/4e03935799fb0c09b126b422aca986cb0d5a8765/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T22:24:49Z","email":"41765025+Kampouse@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jean-philippe Martel"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T22:24:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"nostr plugin parity: KV bindings (challenge/verify) + comments adapters from nearbuilders.org #162 (#6)\n\n* nostr plugin parity: KV bindings (challenge/verify) + comments adapters from nearbuilders.org #162\n\nAdds the nearbuilders.org nostr-bindings and nostr-comments routes as a\nsuperset alongside the existing DB-backed routes, so both plugins can be\nremote-loaded from here:\n\n- BindingService (FastNear KV reads, profile enrichment, challenge/verify,\n  prepare KV write for client-side wallet tx) from plugins/nostr-bindings\n- NostrCommentService (standard/buzz relay adapters, raw query/publish,\n  profile lookup) from plugins/nostr-comments, adapted to the local\n  nostr-core adapters instead of near-nostr-sdk\n\nNew routes (paths + zod shapes identical to the nearbuilders.org contracts):\n  GET  /v1/binding/{nearAccountId}    GET  /v1/identity/{nearAccountId}\n  POST /v1/binding/challenge          POST /v1/binding/verify\n  POST /v1/binding/prepare            GET  /v1/comments\n  POST /v1/comments                   GET  /v1/buzz/channels\n  POST /v1/nostr/query                POST /v1/nostr/publish\n  GET  /v1/nostr/profile/{pubkey}\n\nNew variables: STANDARD_RELAYS, BUZZ_RELAYS, BUZZ_NSEC, KV_API_URL,\nBINDING_CONTRACT, CHALLENGE_EXPIRY_SECONDS.\n\nLegacy DB-backed routes stay functional and are marked DEPRECATED with\ntheir successors; they can be removed once UIs migrate.\n\nNote: upstream nostr-comments referenced an undeclared KV_API in its\nrequireVerified path; declared here so the verified filter actually works.\n\nRef: NEARBuilders/nearbuilders.org#162\n\n* fix: comments as NIP-22 kind 1111 instead of kind 1\n\nKind 1 comments pollute the global nostr feed (every project comment\nappears as a plain note in Damus/Primal, context-free). Comments belong\nin the dedicated NIP-22 comment kind 1111:\n\n- publish: kind 1111 (threading tags unchanged — e/root markers already set)\n- read: kinds [1111, 1] — legacy kind-1 comments keep rendering during\n  migration; drop the kind-1 read once nothing depends on it\n- contract default kind 1 → 1111\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Jean-Philippe Martel <jean-philippe@kampouse.near>","tree":{"sha":"e1e5fcb738c19c04a3e7efed64cfe46b3d3fe61d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/nostr.nearbuilders.org/git/trees/e1e5fcb738c19c04a3e7efed64cfe46b3d3fe61d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/nostr.nearbuilders.org/git/commits/4e03935799fb0c09b126b422aca986cb0d5a8765","verification":{"payload":"tree e1e5fcb738c19c04a3e7efed64cfe46b3d3fe61d\nparent bbd6b2ed076c97d5827019cb89b7196b3fd713a3\nauthor Jean-philippe Martel <41765025+Kampouse@users.noreply.github.com> 1788215089 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788215089 -0500\n\nnostr plugin parity: KV bindings (challenge/verify) + comments adapters from nearbuilders.org #162 (#6)\n\n* nostr plugin parity: KV bindings (challenge/verify) + comments adapters from nearbuilders.org #162\n\nAdds the nearbuilders.org nostr-bindings and nostr-comments routes as a\nsuperset alongside the existing DB-backed routes, so both plugins can be\nremote-loaded from here:\n\n- BindingService (FastNear KV reads, profile enrichment, challenge/verify,\n  prepare KV write for client-side wallet tx) from plugins/nostr-bindings\n- NostrCommentService (standard/buzz relay adapters, raw query/publish,\n  profile lookup) from plugins/nostr-comments, adapted to the local\n  nostr-core adapters instead of near-nostr-sdk\n\nNew routes (paths + zod shapes identical to the nearbuilders.org contracts):\n  GET  /v1/binding/{nearAccountId}    GET  /v1/identity/{nearAccountId}\n  POST /v1/binding/challenge          POST /v1/binding/verify\n  POST /v1/binding/prepare            GET  /v1/comments\n  POST /v1/comments                   GET  /v1/buzz/channels\n  POST /v1/nostr/query                POST /v1/nostr/publish\n  GET  /v1/nostr/profile/{pubkey}\n\nNew variables: STANDARD_RELAYS, BUZZ_RELAYS, BUZZ_NSEC, KV_API_URL,\nBINDING_CONTRACT, CHALLENGE_EXPIRY_SECONDS.\n\nLegacy DB-backed routes stay functional and are marked DEPRECATED with\ntheir successors; they can be removed once UIs migrate.\n\nNote: upstream nostr-comments referenced an undeclared KV_API in its\nrequireVerified path; declared here so the verified filter actually works.\n\nRef: NEARBuilders/nearbuilders.org#162\n\n* fix: comments as NIP-22 kind 1111 instead of kind 1\n\nKind 1 comments pollute the global nostr feed (every project comment\nappears as a plain note in Damus/Primal, context-free). Comments belong\nin the dedicated NIP-22 comment kind 1111:\n\n- publish: kind 1111 (threading tags unchanged — e/root markers already set)\n- read: kinds [1111, 1] — legacy kind-1 comments keep rendering during\n  migration; drop the kind-1 read once nothing depends on it\n- contract default kind 1 → 1111\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Jean-Philippe Martel <jean-philippe@kampouse.near>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlf8xCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJWQQAKF77H9ZtO8hbdl5TdHNZa5w\nj3yScyLQiF9iso/0W/j6SF7E7O5buwnRDSbqPzbVvX2TqW+jKxN0z0ynK+aSxRXt\nOiiAfPibJj4XJNTmy70OzVc4hcHdM3OM3zDHUf3d19va3yZoZqxcH/8M3DZAp0Ry\n6T2QMOQAFWC4vGYpOjlMp1HXwcDPGQQFupsd0y9oIJspWPtL9OLAzpLM9mnrCXpn\n43SG81sg1B2lwSmLUhQeB4ql/VPlsyaUE/VSd13renYfD2lGDxbus03kCyapRzRG\n0PyHCh2kobDq9q/3TDCWl6PDMUQ2e2SxD5sGSJUvttBtrVPzi5zLaa1EjaCQg41c\ngj1bscDbwbsmAxItwKiDOHdc0/XVCIQHCYddp/N4hMXOuJCclUjqmOH+9sCoXhWt\neh7G96y3GNuv4yvin6k+V/Cu85Tiu0dL9h2fcH+fZYGnORJld2FZXkgEujAD/sqD\nPZy5GLcqwOKJcEihYXKD57XNhuJvhMpYwys/+5cdCjiRJXHstgni5cOvcPecq8AE\nVE187AyzXxtNzoYz/F+hB7VQIc6czVidYP2IcdBoMyigrtsLTusqtS+0HYTXIylP\nEntYX1ziikiMKIaAxzZaVr8BfcaswVHel9FecSlL7XSAzkp+SZU0p9OTqX7A6KqT\nZw/JPACyoYgTKYUmLAhr\n=ciSR\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-31T22:24:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/foll